	(text "THE BUS, THE DATA BUFFER, THE PORT DECODE, THE STROBES, THE CONTROL LATCH" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 12.7 0) (effects (font (size 2.5 2.5) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a8501b65-ac65-5cb6-bec6-53ca295b59e9"))
	(text "X1: the YACC1 V3.2 bus (DIN 41612). IC12 stands between the bus's DATA0-7 and the card's ID0-7: towards the card\nbut in a read (-IO-RD), and enabled only while one of the card's ports is addressed (BUFEN, IC13). IC5 decodes\nIO-ADDR0-2 into the eight ports of the card's half (JP3: IO-ADDR3 low or high; JP10: always, or only while -BUS-EN\nis low: the bus tester drives the card with -BUS-EN high); JP4 picks the control port and JP5\nthe data port (port 0 and port 1 in the machine); ports 6 and 7 are the clock's (sheet 6). IC8, open collector with\nRN1: the strobes IO-RD and IO-WR, RESET and -B-RESET, IO-SELDATA. IC10 is the control latch (a write of P0)." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a0f73610-a0b1-5c2a-bcba-becdae5d6712"))
	(embedded_fonts no)
)
